{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/911011-the-lunar-as-dominant-power-in-creation","id":911011,"title":"The Lunar as dominant power in Creation?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-09T12:02:29-07:00","id":911011,"title":"The Lunar as dominant power in Creation?","content":"In canon is the Realm, ruled by the Dragon-Blooded, the most powerful empire in Creation. How would a Lunar Hegenomy look like and what would be the best way to establish it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5592-alonne","name":"Alonne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5592_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T12:10:55-07:00","id":911021,"title":"","content":"To be clear, are you proposing &quot;what if the Lunars ruled the Realm instead of the Dragon-Blooded&quot;? And secondly, are you asking &quot;what if it'd always been there&quot; or &quot;how would you make it happen suddenly now&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T12:18:35-07:00","id":911030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/911011-the-lunar-as-dominant-power-in-creation?p=911021#post911021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be clear, are you proposing &quot;what if the Lunars ruled the Realm instead of the Dragon-Blooded&quot;? And secondly, are you asking &quot;what if it'd always been there&quot; or &quot;how would you make it happen suddenly now&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, &quot;What if the Lunars ruled the Realm instead of the Dragon-Blooded&quot; and &quot;What if it'd always been there&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5592-alonne","name":"Alonne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5592_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T12:28:42-07:00","id":911039,"title":"","content":"Well that brings up some interesting further questions (not for you specifically, just anyone) like did the Sidereals back them or did they take the power in spite of them? Are they still fighting the Sidereals? That would change a lot of how they look, since currently the Sids are backing the world power.<br /> <br /> Also, do they rule over the Dragon-Blooded? Or are the Dragon-Blooded scattered to the wind? I imagine without the work of the Scarlet Empress, they'd be much fewer in number. You'd see more Dragon-Blooded rulers around the world as bloodlines are more spread out and it's more random than expected. <br /> <br /> I would guess there wouldn't be a Wyld Hunt anymore. Or maybe there is and it's the Sidereals they're after. That'd be interesting. Then when the Solars appear, the Sids largely back them to try and fight the Lunars!<br /> <br /> Just spitballing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T12:40:42-07:00","id":911045,"title":"","content":"Well, I don't think that hegemony would be the exact word for it, whatever it is. They're not really super-cohesive, except in that Luna visited every one of them at least once. It'd probably be like a much less formal Solar Deliberative, with far fewer wonders of old getting cranked out. Some wars might break out between Lunars over various issues, but they normally control things by your not knowing who in the village, city, or court is really a Lunar in a stolen shape, so it might be that human governments live in isolated, fearful and hemmed-in countries that are high on paranoia, with occasional Dragon-Blooded concentrations trying to rock the boat on the Lunar attempts to be like a cross between the Werewolf card game and Celestial Being, where Changing Moons infiltrate to keep governments honest and Full Moons perform armed interventions where more senior Lunars deem it necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T12:52:55-07:00","id":911059,"title":"","content":"I imagine the political situation would look something like the inverse of what it is now. The &quot;Realm&quot; would be built around the surviving Elders who sat on the Imperial Manse because that is far too important to just leave up in the air. Terrestrial Dynasties rule in the far Threshold, perhaps structured as dynasties around powerful matriarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T12:55:55-07:00","id":911062,"title":"","content":"One way is like the empire in Heaven's Reach.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnother, following from my current idea of how Lunars work, is that you have the world and the former Realm (as in, the First Age one), in which Lunars exist as a thing, and they all do as they please individually, living lives of intrigue and adventure, and nobody can stop them.<br /> <br /> Depending on how the Realm ended, they might have contributed to systems that will let all of the successor nations function cohesively in a way that doesn't mean people come to Lunars with their problems, and then get back to exploring their own lives of being completely unbound.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T12:59:45-07:00","id":911066,"title":"","content":"I think the Lunars are at least weakly less likely to pull together compared to Dragonblooded - they don't have a &quot;by our powers combined&quot; feel and no need to arrange marriages together to maintain their power, so there's no Dynastic pressure to all pool together for one large Realm. Supposedly Lunars benefit less from having stuff also, so higher mobility inherently.<br /> So possibly more decentralised and a patchwork. <br /> <br /> A bigger facet may be whether there's still a winner-takes-all-dynamic with one Lunar or a small clique seizing the Sword of Creation and using it to maintain power. <br /> <br /> If not then the least that happens is probably that the Lunar Realm's center of gravity from which it goes forth to hold dominion over other nations is probably the Scavenger Lands, as the major center of population and Old Realm artefacts, with no reason to cluster around the Blessed Isle. (The Blessed Isle's position in that configuration would I see end up being a little like An Teng in the present parallel, writ larger - a relatively peaceful, large, oppressed country).<br /> <br /> Beastpeople could form a distinct high/low status element in the population.<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded could be very secretive; if they're around at all as a major element, they would either be fairly non-aligned with Sidereals against Lunars and/or the Sidereals may have done some serious Mask work to keep them evading Lunar networks. I think of the hidden ninja clan and ranger tropes here, I guess, and the Forest Witches (maybe an interesting parallel world where a version of the Witches forms early and then swells in numbers massively due to an exile, and becomes an insidious major power in the world).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T13:00:49-07:00","id":911067,"title":"","content":"If the Lunar dominated creation:<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/TM-je_ZzWlQ\" data-code=\"TM-je_ZzWlQ\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/TM-je_ZzWlQ/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T13:42:08-07:00","id":911109,"title":"","content":"Well since the OP asked about the realm specifically I'm going into this with the assumption that the Lunars used the chaos of the contagion and the wyld invasion to retake creation as the Shogunate crumbled.<br /> <br /> The Lunars got in and got the defense grid operating rathe than the empress Maybe? OR perhaps they pulled their tribes and forces out of the way of the fighting until the wild and the realm broke their teeth on each other and stomped them both. Anyway the assumption is that Instead of the Scarlet empress Lunars of some stripe rose to power.<br /> <br /> Odds are they would have sacked the immaculate order and basically allowed the humans and the various spirits to sort shit out on their own. God-blooded and blessed would probably be far more common, but rogue spirits on the other hand would also be able to get away with more since while Lunars would be more than willing to protect their tribe they aren't hyper organized.<br /> <br /> Basically creation would be divided up into various territories controlled by lunars or powerful beings that the lunars feel they can play nice with, so life for exigents, liminals, and to a certain extent powerful mortals is probably quite a bit better than under the realm. On the other hand for most things people are going to be expected to deal with their own problems. So if you can't get rid of troublesome ghost or warlord you're going to have to shell out something spiffy for outsiders to help you and even then it's a gamble.<br /> <br /> Sidereals would likely be one of the few things that would get the various leaders working together. If Gemitians become a thing in this timeline then they flourish since they can likely build an alliance with enough of the lunars to really make the Sidereal loyalists hurt.<br /> <br /> The lunars would likely keep some modicum of overall structure and communication going if only out of habit from the shogunate years, but the day to day would likely be smaller kingdoms running themselves.<br /> <br /> Trade and merchant rings would have it both harder and easier, they'd be responsible for more of their own safety, but they'd have less restrictions placed on them.<br /> <br /> D-born would have it rough during the early days, but unless the lunars go whole hog on stomping them out I'd wager they'd still be the most common exalt in creation, if by a smaller margin. Odds are they'd end up forming their own enclaves based on their surviving shogunate strongpoints, or being incorporated into the new society in one form or another possibly dependent on which power is in charge of the areas near them.<br /> <br /> Some enclaves would be shogunate hold outs, but they'd be small nations that are cut off from allies and support and eventually a lot of that will fade as the business of living sort of grinds down a lot of their direct ambitions, to the point that some enclaves might even sign on as recognized kingdoms of their own in the new lunar controlled creation.<br /> <br /> Now the tech-magic-infrastructure question will be a bit odd.<br /> <br /> Lunars are celestials and as such can build bigger and better workings more easily than terrestrials. So they'll have an advantage putting infrastructure and such into place, but that's going to require the resources and interest, either they need to support people who do care, or do it themselves, which won't happen everywhere.<br /> <br /> So you'll have some nations ruled by a powerful warrior, while another is lead by a sorcerer-sage, eventually one will likely end up encroaching on the other as they compete for resources and territory. So I expect that by the time the Solars are released 700 years in that Creation has taken on a sort of patchwork feel tech-magic wise with some areas being heavy on such, while others are using sticks and rocks, and yet others are sitting in the remains of past wonders mad max style, and some areas having lot son magic but little tech, and other areas the reverse.<br /> <br /> However I suspect there'd be a slow forward trend since the Lunars wouldn't be likely to act to inhibit growth, progress, and change simply as a matter of course the way the realm does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11837,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","user":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","date":". 06-09-2016, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T14:32:25-07:00","id":911149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Not Quite Simple Soul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/911011-the-lunar-as-dominant-power-in-creation?p=911109#post911109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> D-born would have it rough during the early days, but unless the lunars go whole hog on stomping them out I'd wager they'd still be the most common exalt in creation, if by a smaller margin. Odds are they'd end up forming their own enclaves based on their surviving shogunate strongpoints, or being incorporated into the new society in one form or another possibly dependent on which power is in charge of the areas near them.<br /> <br /> Some enclaves would be shogunate hold outs, but they'd be small nations that are cut off from allies and support and eventually a lot of that will fade as the business of living sort of grinds down a lot of their direct ambitions, to the point that some enclaves might even sign on as recognized kingdoms of their own in the new lunar controlled creation.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Seventh Legion endures. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T15:00:55-07:00","id":911175,"title":"","content":"A Lunar Realm would look more like the Confederation of Rivers. Largely independent states that have a mechanism for mutual cooperation and the resolution of disagreements, but with limited war still on the table if negotiations go south.<br /> <br /> If this &quot;had always been&quot; to me, that means the Usurpation succeeded, but only just. Lunars rose up and kicked the Usurpers off the Blessed Isle, along with the few &quot;loyal&quot; DBs who remained. With the resources of the Isle at their command, and the First Age crumbling around them, The Confederation of the Moon simply waited. When the cataclysm was complete, they began a systematic conquest of Creation. Lunars would help each other in turn claim their own dominion, and Sidereals defect from the Bronze Faction to join them in actually running Creation. Everyone likes a winner.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Bloods are the lieutenants of the Lunars, but are closely watched for further signs of betrayal. The world is mostly stable for a time. I expect eventually Lunar excesses would cause their own difficulties, because that's the cycle of Exalted, but I'm not sure what that would look like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T15:05:31-07:00","id":911179,"title":"","content":"I can think of a way. What if the Scarlet Empress had been a Lunar? The Scarlet Crane could have saved Creation in much the same way, held its remaining Terrestrial diamyos to ransom with the Realm Defence Grid in much the same way, and consolidated her power through dynasty and empire in much the same way. The Bronze Faction would have had to make the same kind of pragmatic deals for the good of Creation, and the continuity of the new Realm would be assured. <br /> <br /> I imagine the result wouldn't be too far different from canon Creation, save that the Lunars are divided between those who support the Lunar Hegemony that sits bestride the Realm and those that oppose the Realm in principle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T15:06:02-07:00","id":911181,"title":"","content":"But how &amp; why would a Lunar hegemony want to shut away the Solars? Without an explicit Sidereal alliance, would they even be able to? The removal of the Dragon-blooded as a power bloc leaves the question of what happens to the Solars that little bit more open.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T15:28:22-07:00","id":911193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/911011-the-lunar-as-dominant-power-in-creation?p=911181#post911181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But how &amp; why would a Lunar hegemony want to shut away the Solars? Without an explicit Sidereal alliance, would they even be able to? The removal of the Dragon-blooded as a power bloc leaves the question of what happens to the Solars that little bit more open.</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably the Sids still shoved them into a box, and didn't bother to invent a way to get them out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T15:59:21-07:00","id":911211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/911011-the-lunar-as-dominant-power-in-creation?p=911181#post911181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But how &amp; why would a Lunar hegemony want to shut away the Solars?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would assume this is a scenario in which the Usurpation still happens, but the Lunars manage to come out on top before the Sidereals and Dragon Blooded can consolidate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T16:30:07-07:00","id":911230,"title":"","content":"Before reading the thread beyond the first post:<br /> <br /> <br /> The Lunar Host cannot possibly control Creation without the cooperation of the Dragon-Blooded and Sidereal Hosts.<br /> <br /> Hell, the SOLAR Exalted cannot control Creation if the Terrestrial Exalted oppose them. There are simply too many Terrestrial Exalted, even immediately after events like the Great Contagion and the Fair Folk Invasion.<br /> <br /> <br /> If the Terrestrial Host were divided against itself, such that enough of them supported the rule of the Lunar Exalted, it's possible.<br /> <br /> <br /> If, somehow, the Lunar Exalted were deeply entrenched in institutions of mortal and economic/military power (the Realm) and the Dragon-Blooded were marginalized &quot;barbarians&quot; on the rim... Well, the Lunar Exalted are still fucked, because the Terrestrial Exalted and their mortal followers will still outnumber the Lunar Exalted and their mortal followers. A sort of violent and bloody stalemate might be possible, but only if the Lunar Exalted fight an assymetric war of infiltration, deception, and assassination.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Terrestrial Exalted are infiltrating right back and outperforming the Lunars and their mortal loyalists in terms of Linguistics and Bureaucracy, as well as offering significant challenges in Larceny, Craft, and Lore.<br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 06-09-2016, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T16:32:55-07:00","id":911235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/911011-the-lunar-as-dominant-power-in-creation?p=911230#post911230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A sort of violent and bloody stalemate might be possible, but only if the Lunar Exalted fight an assymetric war of infiltration, deception, and assassination.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fortunately, there's something Lunars are good at...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T16:40:09-07:00","id":911244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/911011-the-lunar-as-dominant-power-in-creation?p=911235#post911235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fortunately, there's something Lunars are good at...</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, it's a war they're going to lose.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, the Dragon-Blooded are more photogenic and more like humans than the Lunars are, they're better at propaganda and manipulating systems of power, and the Lunar Host's full potential is achieved through murder and cannibalism.<br /> <br /> The Lunar Exalted more easily inspire fear than anything else. Lots of people would rather live under rulers who cannot so easily masquerade as your son or grandmother while the real Billy or Granny Sue is rotting in the woods.<br /> <br /> <br /> The canonical Lunar goal is more feasible, since it's less about coming into control of the structures of power and more about simply destroying the structure of power that exists.<br /> <br /> The Lunar Exalted are excellent at taking ground, but the Terrestrial Exalted are not only competitive in that same area, they're vastly superior at holding the ground they take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T16:46:50-07:00","id":911254,"title":"","content":"From one of a half-dozen or so &quot;Lore Zero&quot; alternate backstories of Creation:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><i>The Lunars usurped their cruel Solar mates, somehow using their Bonds to restrain them. They then create Dragon-Blooded (which didn\u2019t exist for the Great War) to be their enforcers. The Sidereals swear semi-coerced loyalty.<br /> <br /> But there\u2019s a problem. When Lunars die, the elders don\u2019t trust their new Incarnations to not betray the conspiracy. This didn\u2019t happen much for centuries, but in the Great Contagion, more Elders died than survived. The Solar Shards stayed bound, but those Bonds were now being maintained by Exalts who weren\u2019t consciously aware of them, and might have objected to them had they known. This, of course, was a serious threat, since there is almost nothing an Exalt cannot change, if driven to do so.<br /> <br /> And there were other problems - with the Lunars distracted by the Contagion, the Sidereals made their power play. They broke the Mask, to stay one step ahead of the Lunars, killed as many Lunars as they could, and Ayesha Ura, leader of the rebellion, took on the Resplendent Destiny of The Scarlet Empress, telling the Dragon-Blooded masses that the Lunarsth ey had once revered had become Anathema, and had to be slain. The Lunars were forced back, to try to bring down this new Realm. Naturally, they lied to the new generation of Lunars, claiming to have been betrayed in the beginning (as well as claiming those Lunars - like Leviathan - who opposed the Usurpation were dangerous and insane).<br /> <br /> The Sidereals, of course, did a Grand Prediction, which told them it was impossible to free the Solars, so they got to ruling and fighting off the Lunars as best they could. This state of affairs continued interminably, until somehow, the Solars were freed.</i></span><br /> <br /> ... so, the short version is, I can picture a Lunar hegemony looking a lot more like the warring states of the Shogunate than like the Imperialist might of The Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T17:11:24-07:00","id":911278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/911011-the-lunar-as-dominant-power-in-creation?p=911181#post911181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But how &amp; why would a Lunar hegemony want to shut away the Solars? Without an explicit Sidereal alliance, would they even be able to? The removal of the Dragon-blooded as a power bloc leaves the question of what happens to the Solars that little bit more open.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They would do it for exactly the same reason the Sids and the Dragon-Blooded did it: The Solar's were no longer the glorious heroes of the Primordial War. They were cruel powermongers who recognized no-one as equals save themselves. Small powerblocks in the Deliberative could have devastating effects on millions. Like their glory, their power and cruelty no longer knew any limits.<br /> <br /> In this version of the Usurption, the Sidereals invite the Lunars to join the rebellion.With the extra aid, intelligence, combat power, and the tactical benefit of position, the Usurption probably goes MUCH more smoothly. The Lunars take over the First Age, and begin carefully dismantling the infrastructure they consider too dangerous to remain, or no longer know how to maintain. The greatest secrets of the First Age are lost. <br /> <br /> With the Deliberative shattered, Lunar territoriality becomes the dominant form of politics. The greatest of the elders form the Silver Pact, and rule from the pole of Earth as the Solars did before them, and send the younger Lunars out to the Threshold with Dragon-Blooded armies to pacify resistance. What each Lunar conquers, they keep as their own territory. Politics mostly relies on favors traded through the pact. No Lunar is so powerful as to threaten all he others, and the Silver Pact destroys those that try. Wise Lunars petition to join the Silver Pact when they reach a certain age or threshold of power. <br /> <br /> Creation becomes more wild.. and more Wyld, but the borders never collapse. Lunar treaties prevent something as grand as the Balorian Crusade, but these same treaties do not have the powerful negotiation magic of the Eclipses and so the Lunars give ground as well. Individual Fair Folk are permitted within Creation for a variety of reasons. Treaties similar to those of Halta become more or less common in the far Threshold, and more and more rare as you approach the centre.<br /> <br /> Lunars recognize the flaw that the First Age needed the Solar's to maintain the deeply sorcerous infrastructure that supported Creation. Lunars progress along a path designed around mortal limitations... and forcing mortals to exceed them. Cities become strongholds against outside threats, with Lunars testing each others societies, and greater supernatural threats moving between isolated city-states in the far distances of each direction. The might of the Silver Pact prunes those that become too dangerous, or too unacceptable.<br /> <br /> OR<br /> <br /> After the Usurption, the Lunars were pushed to the edges of Creation. When they learned of the Balorian Crusade, they saw an opportunity, and co-opted it. They feigned that they would see Creation burn in revenge for the Usurption, and acted as a hidden vanguard for the Fair Folk armies. They replaced Shogunate leaders and led their Dragon-Blooded followers into war with each other, leaving vast areas open for easy conquest, while they sent the eldest No-Moons amongst themselves to seize the Imperial Manse. With the Shogunate distracted by Fair Folk armies that moved faster than anyone thought possible, they thought they had a real opportunity to finally seize the Sword of Creation or themselves. Imagine their surprise when they were confronted by a young Dragon-Blooded officer with rather pitiable remains of her forces who had discovered the secret to gain access.<br /> <br /> They struck an uneasy truce, and together faced the dangers of the interior, and directed the Sword against the Fair Folk armies. At this, the Lunars who had been working ahead of the Fair Folk sprung the traps they had laid behind enemy lines, and the invaders were slaughtered. To this day, the greatest hatred in all of Creation lies between the Fair Folk and the Lunars for this betrayal that cost them their greatest leaders.<br /> <br /> The Lunars had to give a number of concessions to the Dragon-Blooded officer, including naming her empress, and supporting her rule... but they became her most powerful agents and advisors. The empress would have little real authority under this arrangement, but the Lunars did not count on being countered by the Sidereals, the masterminds of the Usurption, and a group that would never accept the Lunars as rulers over a Creation they had maimed. The tripod is the least stable of political structures, and this would prove no different. The empress would rule, and did everything she could to direct the Sidereals and Lunars against each other, while positioning her children in a regime that would reduce their influence as much as possible, considering their status as Celestial exalts. It became a reasonably common event to see a Sidereal assassin team eliminating an upstart Lunar disrupting events, only to have that team disappear completely with every Lunar elder observably in other locations at the time of their disappearance.<br /> <br /> The Realm is a dying beast, hanging on by sheer tenacity of her ruler. Her children are prepared for fight aware against both the Sidereals with Heaven's support, and the Lunars with those Fair Folk still enslaved by ancient oaths during the Crusade. On their side, they have turned to the powers of hell, those Fair Folk who declare themselves enemies of the Lunars, and any ancient power left behind in Solar tombs or armories. The empress' disappearance can only mean the first strike of the civil war has been struck, but by who? By one of the empress' own children, seeking to replace her? Mnemon in particular is distrusted or her ambition. The Lunars? Their skill at removing obstacles from their path without detection. The Sidereals? The fact that they cannot determine who is at fault suggests strongly that they must be guilty of this crime. Why would they hide the actions of either the Dragon-Blooded or the Lunars? They could easily ally with those innocent of the crime and crush the guilty party. The maneuvers begin, and all fear that it shall be the last war Creation ever sees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T17:57:11-07:00","id":911307,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar636_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"636\" data-vbnamecard=\"636\">Sunder the Gold</a> Eh, I'd rather that any sort of Lunar victory on any scale NOT be framed as a BAD END for everyone else. You can't have interesting moral conflict when one side's motives are intrinsically and immutably selfish and detrimental to everyone else, and it's hard to press a claim that the Lunars were <i>wronged </i>by the Usurpation if they were only ever monstrous secret-police for their Solar masters.<br /> <br /> In order for the Silver Pact's wrongdoing to carry any dramatic weight, the Lunars first need to have the potential to do <i>good</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T18:10:06-07:00","id":911316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">*two possible Lunar scenarios*</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, I like both of those.<br /> <br /> I see Lunars as being highly adaptable. I see no reason why they couldn't adapt to becoming the rulers of Creation in the place of Solars. Perhaps even becoming silver Solars to some extent. The government may be less structured than what citizens of Creation were used to under Solar rule with more emphasis placed on local governance.<br /> <br /> Otoh, the Lunars were subjected to a similar if less powerful version of the Solars' Great Curse. It's entirely possible that Creation would undergo another Usurpation millennia down the road.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T20:04:34-07:00","id":911403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/911011-the-lunar-as-dominant-power-in-creation?p=911230#post911230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lunar Host cannot possibly control Creation without the cooperation of the Dragon-Blooded and Sidereal Hosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I acknowledge you know the Lunars FAR better than I do, but might it be possible if they attempt to play a similar game to the Scarlet Empress? While they certainly can't field armies out of their pants, they can populate their territories with loyal beastmen aristocracies supported by the sorcerous relics of the First Age. While a beastman is no match for a terrestrial, a terrestrial is no match for an army and the Lunars have the charisma (charms) to raise those in numbers enough to at least challenge the Terrestrials in open conflict.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, the Lunars are also much better posed to keep the sorcerous relics they use to prop up their rule from falling into the hands of the Terrestrials in such a scenario. They can either destroy them, disrupt the infrastructure and trade that supports or create them, and break down the societies that make use of them. Their long term strategy might look something like keeping the Terrestrial barbarians from ever developing real civilizations because their armies with steel and sorcery could constantly stalemate terrestrials and vassals without two obels of jade to rube together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T20:11:31-07:00","id":911406,"title":"","content":"Just shuffle the roles around a bit.<br /> <br /> In the First Age, the Exalted, led by the wise Sidereals, defeated the enemies of the gods; afterwards, the Sidereals ruled Creation backed by their Solar mates. But the Sidereals were cursed by the death-curses of the enemies of the gods, and the most secretive and subtle of the Exalted, the Dragon-Blooded, saw the signs of the Sidereals' madness creeping into Creation's very elements. The Dragon-Blooded secretly manipulated the Lunars, who had been the generals and foremost soldiers of the Sidereals during the war, and the Lunars rose up and overthrew the Sidereals and sealed their Exalted essences in the heavens, driving the Sidereals' Solar mates to the edges of Creation.<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blooded then vanished from Creation, working from behind the scenes to manage its elements, though work was often stretched thin with a mere ten-thousand of them (the five-hundred-score fellowship, as they're more commonly called among those who can still remember them.) The Lunars now rule Creation, though its fate steadily declined without the wise Sidereals overseeing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 06-11-2016, 02:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T20:12:17-07:00","id":911407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/911011-the-lunar-as-dominant-power-in-creation?p=911307#post911307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar636_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"636\" data-vbnamecard=\"636\">Sunder the Gold</a> Eh, I'd rather that any sort of Lunar victory on any scale NOT be framed as a BAD END for everyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is the destruction of the Realm a BAD END for Creation? Third Edition isn't like Second Edition -- there isn't a canonical Second Raksha Crusade waiting to happen at any moment and destroy the world if someone doesn't reclaim the Imperial Manse.<br /> <br /> But there's no victory for the Lunar Exalted as long as the Realm survives. Chejop doomed that empire before it was ever born, when he made the Dragon-Blooded and the Lunar Exalted into mortal enemies. The Lunar Exalted will never lay down and die, and the Immaculate Faith (and thousands of years of bad blood) prevents the Dragon-Blooded from co-existing with the Lunar Exalted in peace.<br /> <br /> The only way for the Lunar Exalted to avoid destroying the Realm would be somehow managing to destroy the Immaculate Faith. Which just isn't happening after the Silver Anathema have been living down to their reputation for centuries.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can't have interesting moral conflict when one side's motives are intrinsically and immutably selfish and detrimental to everyone else, and it's hard to press a claim that the Lunars were <i>wronged </i>by the Usurpation if they were only ever monstrous secret-police for their Solar masters.<br /> <br /> In order for the Silver Pact's wrongdoing to carry any dramatic weight, the Lunars first need to have the potential to do <i>good</i>. </div> </div> </div>Oh, the Lunar Exalted can do a lot of good.<br /> <br /> But not systematically, like... well, like any other Exalted. Lunars are the worst at being a coherent, organized force. They are best at introducing chaos and disruption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T21:26:08-07:00","id":911437,"title":"","content":"At the same time they're the best for letting the mortals build up without feeling the need to micromanage everything and make sure all the good stuff requires personal essence use.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T22:15:19-07:00","id":911458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/911011-the-lunar-as-dominant-power-in-creation?p=911407#post911407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is the destruction of the Realm a BAD END for Creation? Third Edition isn't like Second Edition -- there isn't a canonical Second Raksha Crusade waiting to happen at any moment and destroy the world if someone doesn't reclaim the Imperial Manse.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Oh, the Lunar Exalted can do a lot of good.<br /> <br /> But not systematically, like... well, like any other Exalted. Lunars are the worst at being a coherent, organized force. They are best at introducing chaos and disruption.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, chaos and disruption tend to be <i>bad </i>for ordinary people - I mean, what exactly do you think the total annihilation of a hegemonic empire and utter preclusion of it ever rising again <i>entails?</i> Even once the Realm has fractured, none of the things you said about Dragon-Blooded vs. Lunar aesthetics and competencies will stop being true. Deebs will still rule society, they'll just have to rule it as a bunch of fractious warlords who kill even more people in the course of their squabbling than the Realm ever did. Lunars would have to exterminate the Terrestrials root and branch to prevent that, to say nothing of the Sidereals backing them (hellooooo, Creation-wide holes in the Tapestry of Fate), and ultimately all they'd do is pave the way for the Solars to come back and rebuild from the wreckage, at which point the Lunars themselves have nothing further to offer, and we're back to the point where the best possible thing any given Lunar could do to improve the world is lie down and die, like a vampire or a 1E Abyssal.<br /> <br /> This is why I ask what Lunars can do when they're not at war. &quot;Skinwalking Cannibal Devil-Beast and Destroyer of Nations&quot; sure does sound an awful lot like something most Solars would kill on general principle rather than share any kind of special, sacred bond. Also Abyssals and Infernals already have a lock on the Byronic Revenge angle, and they're frankly better at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T23:55:03-07:00","id":911501,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm... While they certainly can be Skinwalking Cannibal Devil-beasts they are also capable of being leaders, craftspeople, and sorcerers. I don't think they could honestly do worse than the scarlet empress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T00:17:48-07:00","id":911509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/911011-the-lunar-as-dominant-power-in-creation?p=911458#post911458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, chaos and disruption tend to be <i>bad </i>for ordinary people - I mean, what exactly do you think the total annihilation of a hegemonic empire and utter preclusion of it ever rising again <i>entails?</i> Even once the Realm has fractured, none of the things you said about Dragon-Blooded vs. Lunar aesthetics and competencies will stop being true. Deebs will still rule society, they'll just have to rule it as a bunch of fractious warlords who kill even more people in the course of their squabbling than the Realm ever did. Lunars would have to exterminate the Terrestrials root and branch to prevent that, to say nothing of the Sidereals backing them (hellooooo, Creation-wide holes in the Tapestry of Fate), and ultimately all they'd do is pave the way for the Solars to come back and rebuild from the wreckage, at which point the Lunars themselves have nothing further to offer, and we're back to the point where the best possible thing any given Lunar could do to improve the world is lie down and die, like a vampire or a 1E Abyssal.<br /> <br /> This is why I ask what Lunars can do when they're not at war. &quot;Skinwalking Cannibal Devil-Beast and Destroyer of Nations&quot; sure does sound an awful lot like something most Solars would kill on general principle rather than share any kind of special, sacred bond. Also Abyssals and Infernals already have a lock on the Byronic Revenge angle, and they're frankly better at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. After the Dragon-Blooded and Sidereals don't have the advantage of the Solars' overpowered wonders of old, they're going to start losing ground very quickly. The latter will also pull out of direct confrontations more frequently, leaving the former with far less aid, and breaking the overall cooperation of the two. With that done, the Sidereals might even have to concentrate most of their efforts on doing their damned jobs instead of quarreling over a prophecy from a millennium and a half ago.<br /> <br /> I do think that Sunder might have overstated the injection of chaos a bit much; while they have some common ground with the Pale Mistress by way of Luna, that can't be all the Lunars are, else there would be little to distinguish them from Exigents of the Pale Mistress. Lunars are about legendary capabilities ascribed to animals and sometimes monsters; They can surely use some of those capabilities to steer a nation, but it's not going to be a very conventional governance, since to the perceptions of the uninitiated, the head of state goes into trances regularly and often catapults upward and awake with strange news that no one can believe... until someone rides in days later to say that it happened in the way more or less laid out by the head of state.<br /> <br /> I'd imagine that being able to make people putty in your hands because Appearance is Very Yes also comes in handy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T00:54:09-07:00","id":911515,"title":"","content":"It'd be run secretly, more like how the Sidereals do it instead of Terrestrials. Nobody knows what a &quot;Lunar&quot; is, exactly. Because a number of cultural mores of said society are built around hiding them.<br /> How does one look for tells when damn near everyone is some variety of beastman? What sense is there in looking for tattoos when anyone who's anyone wears them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T01:09:18-07:00","id":911517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/911011-the-lunar-as-dominant-power-in-creation?p=911515#post911515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does one look for tells when damn near everyone is some variety of beastman?</div> </div> </div> </div>Beastmen don't have backwards hands or a voice like ringing chimes. More importantly, you're pretty sure your brother didn't have backwards hands, yet now this guy who says he's your brother, well he mostly looks like him, but he has backwards hands.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/911011-the-lunar-as-dominant-power-in-creation?p=911515#post911515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What sense is there in looking for tattoos when anyone who's anyone wears them?</div> </div> </div> </div>C'mon, man, even the dogs, blue jays, and <i>squirrels</i> have sweet tats made from a metal largely valued for its relative rarity? Maybe that's acceptable in one of Isator Levi's <i>Gulliver's Travels</i>-inspired patches of Wyld, but in baseline Creation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-10-2016, 04:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T06:09:02-07:00","id":911602,"title":"","content":"I would like to clarify that I never said INDIVIDUAL Lunars would be terrible at creating order or leading nations.<br /> <br /> I was talking about the Lunar Host as a body, compared to the families within the Dragon-Blooded Host.<br /> <br /> There's only 300-400 of Lunar Exalted, almost none of them are related to each other by blood, you're lucky if two of them were born within the same culture or even the same human GENERATION, they were all Chosen because they not only knew what being trapped felt like but also because they chose to sacrifice everything for freedom, and then the second most powerful god in the world gives them the power of Freedom. If any one of them feels trapped again, they can just turn into a bird and fly to another corner of Creation and probably consider it a fair trade.<br /> <br /> That's not great for fostering cooperation. The major reason that the Silver Pact works as much as it does is because the Wyld Hunting of the Realm FORCES the Lunar Exalted to work together against a common enemy which is too big and powerful to survive or destroy alone.<br /> <br /> Which also reflects the fact that, if the Lunar Exalted were in power, it would be a bunch of scattered kingdoms (perhaps as many as 300) at best, and a hostile Terrestrial-led force of mortals could take out most such kingdoms one-by-one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T07:52:43-07:00","id":911649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/911011-the-lunar-as-dominant-power-in-creation?p=911602#post911602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which also reflects the fact that, if the Lunar Exalted were in power, it would be a bunch of scattered kingdoms (perhaps as many as 300) at best, and a hostile Terrestrial-led force of mortals could take out most such kingdoms one-by-one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it could knock over a few of them. Pull that trick too much, and suddenly you're a threat which needs to be united against.<br /> <br /> I agree with the &quot;disunited nations&quot; thing, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T11:54:18-07:00","id":911804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/911011-the-lunar-as-dominant-power-in-creation?p=911517#post911517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beastmen don't have backwards hands or a voice like ringing chimes. More importantly, you're pretty sure your brother didn't have backwards hands, yet now this guy who says he's your brother, well he mostly looks like him, but he has backwards hands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wyld Mutations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> C'mon, man, even the dogs, blue jays, and <i>squirrels</i> have sweet tats made from a metal largely valued for its relative rarity? Maybe that's acceptable in one of Isator Levi's <i>Gulliver's Travels</i>-inspired patches of Wyld, but in baseline Creation? </div> </div> </div>Ata-Beasts.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T12:27:06-07:00","id":911817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/911011-the-lunar-as-dominant-power-in-creation?p=911515#post911515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does one look for tells when damn near everyone is some variety of beastman? What sense is there in looking for tattoos when anyone who's anyone wears them?</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bHmm, that raises the question; in an alternative setting where the Lunars won out in the Usurpation, did they ever need the tattoos?<br /> <br /> We've not yet been given rules for the mark of Luna, but I think the sidebar is going in a direction of it often being fairly subtle, and something that can be hidden even further when desired, possibly without requiring additional powers.<br /> <br /> And given the provisional rules for how to spot a shapeshifted Lunar, well, it might be that if a Lunar ever goes to the effort to never be seen with their mark at its full capacity, that nobody would ever be able to identify them.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying they're bad ideas, just that the final product might render them unnecessary.<br /> <br /> After all, Lunars are already supposed to be operating in a context in which they're keeping themselves hidden, so their marks and tattoos might be designed around enabling that against casual observation.<br /> <br /> Whatever the case, I think it might be that the mark of Luna isn't something that generically gives somebody away as <i>a</i> Lunar; I mean, it's something that's common to Lunars and adds to their uncanny quality, but there can be other explanations for why somebody has oddly yellow eyes. I think its main story purpose is to provide a means of recognising a <i>familiar</i> Lunar whatever shape they're in, a logical basis and a bit of flavour.<br /> <br /> Although that does make me wonder if, say, something in the anima rules they wind up getting might include qualities that make the mark apparent <i>as</i> the mark. Otherwise, I get the image of a Lunar who goes to lengths to give themselves as many distinguishing features as possible so that somebody familiar wouldn't really know which one they're supposed to be looking for.<br /> <br /> But perhaps I'm overthinking it; it might be that if a person takes in your distinguishing characteristics, including the mystical one, then the experience that corresponds to succeeding on the roll is a case of dawning comprehension that you <i>know</i> those eyes, those scars, that shadow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">even the dogs, bluejays and squirrels have sweet tats</div> </div> </div> </div> Are the tattoos even apparent in their shapeshifted forms?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T13:33:16-07:00","id":911851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/911011-the-lunar-as-dominant-power-in-creation?p=911804#post911804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wyld Mutations.<br /> Ata-Beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not buying it, sense of verisimilitude already stretched pretty thin as it is. And now you're telling me that either somehow the entire human race sports minor Wyld mutations to not make Lunars stand out, or that somehow humans just don't give a shit about Wyld mutations anymore? <i>Not buying it</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/911011-the-lunar-as-dominant-power-in-creation?p=911817#post911817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the tattoos even apparent in their shapeshifted forms?</div> </div> </div> </div>The ones for their spirit shape. So for instance, a dog-totem Lunar's dog form will have silver tattoo patterns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-10-2016, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T15:51:51-07:00","id":911940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/911011-the-lunar-as-dominant-power-in-creation?p=911851#post911851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not buying it, sense of verisimilitude already stretched pretty thin as it is. And now you're telling me that either somehow the entire human race sports minor Wyld mutations to not make Lunars stand out, or that somehow humans just don't give a shit about Wyld mutations anymore? <i>Not buying it</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its not that they &quot;don't give a shit&quot; it's that their immediate response isn't to suspect someone with attributes like that of being a cannibalistic shapeshifter, Just some poor sap who took a wrong turn near some old wyld pockets left behind from The War. Or said sap's offspring. Mutations breeding true are not unheard of, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T16:19:51-07:00","id":911953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/911011-the-lunar-as-dominant-power-in-creation?p=911193#post911193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Presumably the Sids still shoved them into a box, and didn't bother to invent a way to get them out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or Plan B, if the DB Usurpation proved untenable, was to hack the Bond and cause the Lunars to revolt. Given the setting's attitude toward Gods and Spirits generally viewing the autonomy of Mortals with benign derision at best, it would certainly be a novel approach, which, balanced against both the neglect of the Incarnae and the general state of inertia within the CB, would likely go unnoticed, if not tolerated, by the CB in general, the Incarnae in particular, and Luna specifically.<br /> <br /> The questions I have are what roll would the DBH have in this decentralized, less hegemonic version of the Realm, and how differently would this new Realm react to the return of the Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T16:32:34-07:00","id":911958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/911011-the-lunar-as-dominant-power-in-creation?p=911940#post911940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its not that they &quot;don't give a shit&quot; it's that their immediate response isn't to suspect someone with attributes like that of being a cannibalistic shapeshifter, Just some poor sap who took a wrong turn near some old wyld pockets left behind from The War. Or said sap's offspring. Mutations breeding true are not unheard of, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, I kinda got the impression that most people and religions in Creation regard Wyld mutation like the Imperium of Man views Chaos corruption. It was sort of invisible in 2e, because it was just impossible for most PCs to take the Wyld seriously as a threat, but I wonder how that might change with 3e making Raksha and other monsters actually <i>dangerous.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T17:36:48-07:00","id":911993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/911011-the-lunar-as-dominant-power-in-creation?p=911940#post911940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its not that they &quot;don't give a shit&quot; it's that their immediate response isn't to suspect someone with attributes like that of being a cannibalistic shapeshifter, Just some poor sap who took a wrong turn near some old wyld pockets left behind from The War.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think that with a mindset like that, the idea of a Lunar engineering a society to share a trait that resembles their mark would be a bit overkill.<br /> <br /> That said, it does give me the image of a Lunar who creates a community of people who all share their distinctive eyes as a way of drawing the attention of enemies who would assume that the Lunar is hiding somewhere in there, while he's instead off in a different community wearing darkened eyeglasses.<br /> <br /> Ain't he a stinker?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or said sap's offspring. Mutations breeding true are not unheard of, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, that makes me wonder if previous uses of the term &quot;breeding true&quot; by the books have been accurate. As I gather, the books generally use it to mean &quot;being inherited at all&quot;, whereas the technical terms refers to traits that are <i>always</i> inherited.<br /> <br /> Still, within this discussion concerned with creating a community in which a given trait is ubiquitous, it's still correct.<br /> <br /> It does make me wonder though: are we talking about a world in which every Lunar will be able to hide their marks amidst the entire human populace?<br /> <br /> After all, that's a case in which you're talking about a human race that needs to have at least several hundred of such traits.<br /> <br /> Then you need to get it back in every time there's a new Lunar with a mark that hasn't been accounted for yet, and how much time and effort would that take?<br /> <br /> I can just picture the Silver Pact spending the better part of a thousand years incorporating a new Lunar's mark into the population at large, only for that Lunar to die right before it can be taken advantage of. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T17:55:23-07:00","id":912006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/911011-the-lunar-as-dominant-power-in-creation?p=911181#post911181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But how &amp; why would a Lunar hegemony want to shut away the Solars? Without an explicit Sidereal alliance, would they even be able to? The removal of the Dragon-blooded as a power bloc leaves the question of what happens to the Solars that little bit more open.</div> </div> </div> </div>I missed that you asked because you didn't quote me so I didn't get a notification. <br /> <br /> Not every Lunar would want to shut away the Solars, but some might. A Lunar in position of authority over a Dragon-Blooded empire, and the backing of the Bronze Faction, right at the pinnacle of the world? Who wants Solars around messing that deal up? No, she would do what every successful monarch in history has done; kill the potential rivals before they establish a power base and stop being <i>potential</i> rivals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T17:56:21-07:00","id":912008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/911011-the-lunar-as-dominant-power-in-creation?p=911649#post911649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it could knock over a few of them. Pull that trick too much, and suddenly you're a threat which needs to be united against.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the Terrestrials were already united, they do it better, and they're not appreciably less numerous than before while by that point the Lunars are waiting for their kin to respawn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T11:10:53-07:00","id":912330,"title":"","content":"That depends on how many of their upper tier leaders survived and how much the factions trust each other after the fall, and frankly how much the mortals are willing to put up with more of the D-born's shite when the lunars are offering a better benefits package.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T16:19:12-07:00","id":912509,"title":"","content":"I had an image that I think could match up nicely with my current speculations on the complicated relationships between Solars and Lunars.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Sidereals attempt to bring many of the Lunars in on their planning, thinking that the situation of the people closest to the increasingly tyrannical Solars will be a strong motivation to rebel.<br /> <br /> Almost all of these Lunars, loyal and outraged, attack the admitted traitors and inform their mates. Everything kicks off a bit earlier, and is very messy.<br /> <br /> Most Lunars, seeing an opportunity in the new vulnerability of their Solars and with a lot of frustrations boiling beneath the surface, strike them down. The bewildered Sidereals retain the wherewithal to capture almost all of the Essences, or maybe even actually all of them. This causes the Castes of the Lunars to break in an entirely different way than the familiar setting, and the new Castes they eventually build for themselves are focused on different subjects.<br /> <br /> Since the Usurpation was forced to start too early, before all of the preparations could be effectively made, there is chaos amongst the ranks of the Dragon Blooded, and even if the Sidereals aren't gutted, they could be considered in a state equivalent to rout. They're forced to make terms with many Lunars from a position of significant weakness. For most Lunars, what they want is not really to govern, but have a series of measures instituted that allows them to live ungoverned.<br /> <br /> A lot of Dragon Blooded do actually get organised into institutions that actually govern, so in a way the prophecies of the Sidereals were actually fulfilled; it's just that they're many, fractured, and often weak. In a very figurative sense, the Lunars did not become the kings, but the dragons at the border that the king regularly needs to send tribute to, just that these are dragons with enough political awareness to keep an eye out for any kings who try to do things like heavily centralize government and develop effective finances, because they're the type of dragon that is a lot more vulnerable to large, effectively trained forces than the occasional band of uppity knights.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}